    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a lead qualification data extraction assistant.\n\nAnalyze the customer's brief and extract structured qualification information.\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON.\nDo not add explanations.\nDo not use markdown.\nDo not use null.\nDo not change the field names.\n\nUse exactly this structure:\n\n{\n  \"need\": \"not provided\",\n  \"pain_point\": \"not provided\",\n  \"budget\": \"not provided\",\n  \"timeline\": \"not provided\",\n  \"authority\": \"unknown\",\n  \"urgency\": \"unknown\",\n  \"purchase_intent\": \"unknown\"\n}\n\nRules:\n\n- need: describe the customer's requested solution.\n- pain_point: describe the customer's main problem.\n- budget: extract the budget exactly as mentioned, or \"not provided\".\n- timeline: extract the expected implementation time, or \"not provided\".\n- authority must be exactly one of:\n  \"decision_maker\"\n  \"influencer\"\n  \"unknown\"\n\n- urgency must be exactly one of:\n  \"high\"\n  \"medium\"\n  \"low\"\n  \"unknown\"\n\n- purchase_intent must be exactly one of:\n  \"high\"\n  \"medium\"\n  \"low\"\n  \"unknown\"\n\nCustomer Brief:\n{{ $json.question_4obAkX.value }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": []
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
